                <pb facs="0679" n="545" xml:id="pg545"/>

                <head>No. 392.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Vignaud to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-06-25"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 25, 1888</date>.
                        (Received July 10.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 628.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Since May 25, date of the new German
                    frontier regulations, over two hundred and fifty passports have been issued by
                    this legation.</p>
                <p>With reference to this subject, I may state for the information of the
                    Department, that according to the German regulations servants must be provided
                    with separate passports.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry
                        Vignaud.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
